General idea is to use a classic get/put based circular fifo with one empty slot.

But since this supports multiple producers/consumers, instead of adding data in place
then incrementing put pointer (and consuming in place of get and incrementing after
consumption) we ll pull some tricks using dwCAS.

dwCAS __IS NOT__ DCAS!!

On x86_64 its the lock:cmpxchg16B instruction that takes a 16B aligned pointer and CASes
two adjacent 8B dwords. The real DCAS expects to be able to do this on non contiguous 
memory.


