 IMPORTANT PLEASE READ:
 Modified algorithm no longer requires
 dwCAS. CAS on put / get individually is sufficient. 

 For the producer you can read get and put once and run full condition
 check on cached values. Nothing consumer does can induce a full condition
 so cached value of GET is good enough. However other concurrent producers
 could induce a full condition so you try to CAS an increment of PUT. 

 Consumer follows similar logic with the GET pointer.

 UPDATE: 
 This still suffers from the ABA problem. 
 localPut = PUT(fifo);
 ... between this and the CAS the put pointer could do a full 
     circle and come back to the same PUT value.

 I would argue it is still not a problem. There is no value associated
 with the PUT value so its functionally still correct since no other 
 producer thread claims ownership to this value of PUT.
